@format 1
@id tabs.relay-out
@title Relay tab to another process
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Detect a tab dropped outside the application, serialize it, deliver it to a process under the drop point when available, or launch a new receiver.
@section I. UI
@tabs Global interface
@flow TB
@related relay.receive-tab

@alias toolbar = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PToolbar

[input] Tab drag released <input>
- Check whether the released tab lies outside the current application window @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
> eligible

[eligible] Check relay eligibility <decision>
- Reject a drop inside the window or a busy tab @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
? "Relay is not allowed" > unchanged
? "Tab can leave this process" > serialize

[serialize] Save relay payload <storage>
- Serialize the tab state to a relay file @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
> target

[target] Find a receiver under the drop point <decision>
- Find an existing Cadroue process at the released screen position @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
? "Receiving process found" > deliver
? "No receiving process found" > launch

[deliver] Deliver to existing process <process>
- Send the saved relay-file path through that process's relay channel @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
? "Delivery accepted" > close
? "Delivery refused" > unchanged

[launch] Start a new receiving process <external>
- Start Cadroue with the relay-file argument @ toolbar.PTabRelayStart(...)
? "Process started" > close
? "Launch failed" > unchanged

[close] Close originating tab <process>
- Close the tab only after a live delivery or new-process launch succeeds @ toolbar.PTabRelayCheck(...)
> result

[result] Tab relayed <output>
= The receiving process obtains the serialized tab state.

[unchanged] Tab retained <output>
= The tab remains in the current process.
